# Web3Forms access key — relays the contact form to your inbox.
# Get one free at https://web3forms.com (enter your email, it's mailed to you).
#
# The VITE_ prefix is required: Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to
# client code, and the browser has to carry this key. Web3Forms' free tier
# rejects server-to-server calls (403, "use our API in client side"), so there
# is no way to keep it server-side short of their Pro plan.
#
# That makes it public — readable in the bundle and in the Network tab. It is a
# public identifier rather than a secret: the only thing it can do is deliver
# mail to the inbox that created it. Never put an actual secret behind VITE_.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in, then set the same variable in your host's
# environment (Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables).
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
